Keep liblldb's embedded LLVM private to liblldb.

liblldb-private.exports exports _ZN4llvm* from liblldb, which is upstream's
design: liblldb is the one LLVM provider for the lldb tool family, and the
drivers import llvm symbols from it. That design and a shared libLLVM.dylib
cannot share a process. Both images export the same weak vague-linkage
symbols -- template instantiations, class-static registry members -- and dyld
coalesces them, so the two copies' registries unify while each copy's static
initializers still run: the second registration of 'basic' (RegAllocBasic)
aborts the debugger at plugin load, inside dyld, before any breakpoint.

    LLVM ERROR: Option 'basic' already exists!

Dropping the llvm patterns demotes every llvm symbol in liblldb to private
extern at link (-exported_symbols_list demotes what it does not match, weak
included), so there is no exported twin to coalesce with and each copy keeps
its own registries. The overlay's drivers are unaffected: lldb, lldb-dap and
lldb-argdumper each already link //llvm:Option and //llvm:Support statically,
which is where their llvm references resolve.

lldb:: and lldb_private:: stay exported exactly as before.

diff --git a/lldb/source/API/liblldb-private.exports b/lldb/source/API/liblldb-private.exports
--- a/lldb/source/API/liblldb-private.exports
+++ b/lldb/source/API/liblldb-private.exports
@@ -3,9 +3,6 @@ _ZNK4lldb*
 _ZN12lldb_private*
 _ZNK12lldb_private*
 _ZTVN12lldb_private*
-_ZN4llvm*
-_ZNK4llvm*
-_ZTVN4llvm*
 init_lld*
 PyInit__lldb*
 luaopen_lldb*
